#1.3 Blockquotes & Embedded Blocks 

abstract art 

> Single-line level 1 quote.

> Multi-line level 1 quote.
> Second line of the same quote.
>> Nested level 2 quote.
>>> Deeply nested level 3 quote.
>> Back to level 2 quote.
> Back to level 1 quote.

Quote with embedded code block (The bug you just hit!):
> Here is code inside a quote:
> <!python: quoted_math.py
def calculate_buoyancy(mass_kg: float, volume_m3: float) -> float:
    RHO_WATER = 1025.0  # kg/m^3
    return (volume_m3 * RHO_WATER) - mass_kg
!>
> And here is prose immediately following the quoted code block.

Quote with inline formatting and links:
> As stated in [https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2%20Samuel%206%3A14&version=ESV| 2 Samuel 6:14]: 
>> And David danced before the Lord with all his might. And David was wearing a linen ephod.

#1.4 List Hierarchy, Auto-Counters & Coordinate Algebra

Explicit list with gutter attachments:
1. Explicit item number 1
| Attached gutter paragraph 1.
| Attached gutter paragraph 2 with `inline code` and **bold**.
| <!c:gutter_code.c
void march(void) {
    printf("Horses are horsing around...\n");
}
!>
| Final attached gutter paragraph.

Auto-increment lists (Counter continuation after explicit 1):
+ First auto-item (should render 2.)
+ Second auto-item (should render 3.)
  +.+ Nested numeric depth two (should render 3.1.)
  +.+ Nested numeric depth two sibling (should render 3.2.)
    +.+.+ Nested numeric depth three (should render 3.2.1.)
  +.+ Back to depth two (should render 3.3.)
+ Back to depth one (should render 4.)

Coordinate type switching:
- Lower alpha item a (should render a.)
- Lower alpha item b (should render b.)
  -.- Nested lower alpha (should render b.a.)
  -.- Nested lower alpha sibling (should render b.b.)

Upper alpha and Roman coordinates:
^ Upper alpha 1 (should render A.)
^ Upper alpha 2 (should render B.)
= Roman numeral 1 (should render i.)
= Roman numeral 2 (should render ii.)

Mixed coordinate algebra:
+.+.- Mixed numeric-alpha coordinate (should render 1.1.a.)
+.+.= Mixed numeric-roman coordinate (should render 1.1.i.)
+.+.^ Mixed numeric-upper coordinate (should render 1.1.A.)

Unordered bullet list with whitespace depth:
* Bullet depth 1
  * Bullet depth 2 via 2 spaces
    * Bullet depth 3 via 4 spaces
* Back to bullet depth 1

Boundary : Bold at line-start must NOT be parsed as a bullet list:
**This is bold text at column 0, NOT a bullet list.**

