#1.6 Code Blocks 

Code block with title and language:
<!rust:lexer_core.rs
use logos::Logos;

#[derive(Logos, Debug, PartialEq)]
pub enum Token<'a> {
    #[token("<!")]
    CodeBlockStart,
    #[regex(r"[a-zA-Z_]+")]
    Ident(&'a str),
}
!>

Code block with language only (no title, should push lang tag to the right):
<!python
import sys

def main():
    print(f"Python version: {sys.version}")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
!>

Code block with title only (no language):
<!:Plain Notes
Just some arbitrary notes without a language identifier.
Indentation should be preserved verbatim:
    four spaces
        eight spaces
!>

Code block with custom delimiter (contains `!>` inside the code!):
<!bash:deploy.sh|CUSTOM_FENCE
#!/usr/bin/env bash
echo "This contains a raw closing tag: !> right here!"
echo "And another one: !>"
!CUSTOM_FENCE>

Code block with tricky characters and HTML injection attempts:
<!html:xss_test.html
<script>alert("XSS attempt");</script>
<div class="test" data-val="&quot;&amp;&lt;&gt;">
    <p>Safe & sound</p>
</div>
!>

